(1443579, 186856, 24991, '<td valign="top">I like how the yellow ladder adds contrast to this otherwise boring shot.  8 by me!</td>', 'I like how the yellow ladder adds contrast to this otherwise boring shot.  8 by me!', '2005-06-09 12:18:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(1443581, 186843, 24991, '<td valign="top">In my opinion, the title is a little bit weak, but I like the colors in your shot, the yellow on the CAT is perticularily nice!</td>', 'In my opinion, the title is a little bit weak, but I like the colors in your shot, the yellow on the CAT is perticularily nice!', '2005-06-09 12:19:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(1443584, 186774, 24991, '<td valign="top">Woah!  Crazy title, and extremely good perspective on an issue that is clearly pertinant in this construction zone.  I gave this shot a 9 if nothing else for your great connotations behind the title.</td>', 'Woah!  Crazy title, and extremely good perspective on an issue that is clearly pertinant in this construction zone.  I gave this shot a 9 if nothing else for your great connotations behind the title.', '2005-06-09 12:21:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(1443586, 185956, 30929, '<td valign="top">great clouds, but the cement boom arm in the middle takes away from the shot.</td>', 'great clouds, but the cement boom arm in the middle takes away from the shot.', '2005-06-09 12:21:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(1443588, 186789, 24991, '<td valign="top">Great contrasting between lights and darks!</td>', 'Great contrasting between lights and darks!', '2005-06-09 12:21:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(1443592, 186848, 24991, '<td valign="top">I know what idea you''re going for, with the sun flare in the shot, but I think it takes away from the shot becuase it causes you to use an exposure that is so fast that it makes the house, wich should be the primary subject of the photograph, rather dark.  If this was the idea that you were going for, it might have been slightly better to use an even faster shutter speed and go for an all-out silloette of the building, and possibly then put it in black and white and up the contrast to eliminate any residual grayscale on the house...Just a thought.</td>', 'I know what idea you''re going for, with the sun flare in the shot, but I think it takes away from the shot becuase it causes you to use an exposure that is so fast that it makes the house, wich should be the primary subject of the photograph, rather dark.  If this was the idea that you were going for, it might have been slightly better to use an even faster shutter speed and go for an all-out silloette of the building, and possibly then put it in black and white and up the contrast to eliminate any residual grayscale on the house...Just a thought.', '2005-06-09 12:24:18.000000', NULL, 1),
