(1456928, 186128, 38119, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the comments everyone. I know the shot was far from perfect, so thanks to everyone that gave me feedback on what they liked or didn''t like about it. :)</td>', 'Thanks for the comments everyone. I know the shot was far from perfect, so thanks to everyone that gave me feedback on what they liked or didn''t like about it. :)', '2005-06-15 06:04:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(1456930, 184893, 19746, '<td valign="top">Good going, Nico!  Rack up those ribbons :)<br/> <br/>Congratulations - I didn''t vote on this challenge (exams etc.) but this is a truly fantastic shot.  How much PP did you do?  I love that effect - really cool.  Good vision to see the potential of the reflection.  I''ll warrant you also cut out some unsightly aspects of the composition (buildings, telephone lines etc.) and squared the shot away nicely with the railings - cunning plan, there.<br/> <br/>Congrats again,<br/>Alex</td>', 'Good going, Nico!  Rack up those ribbons :) Congratulations - I didn''t vote on this challenge (exams etc.) but this is a truly fantastic shot.  How much PP did you do?  I love that effect - really cool.  Good vision to see the potential of the reflection.  I''ll warrant you also cut out some unsightly aspects of the composition (buildings, telephone lines etc.) and squared the shot away nicely with the railings - cunning plan, there. Congrats again,Alex', '2005-06-15 06:05:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(1456933, 185713, 19746, '<td valign="top">Great capture of this wirey old builder.  I like the way this is composed and I think the B&amp;W works pretty well here.  Congrats on your ribbon :)<br/> <br/>Alex</td>', 'Great capture of this wirey old builder.  I like the way this is composed and I think the B&W works pretty well here.  Congrats on your ribbon :) Alex', '2005-06-15 06:07:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(1456939, 186940, 27845, '<td valign="top">I find your post processing skills very impressive. You created a great mood, one which I could barely have seen in the original. Thanks for sharing.</td>', 'I find your post processing skills very impressive. You created a great mood, one which I could barely have seen in the original. Thanks for sharing.', '2005-06-15 06:09:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(1456945, 186886, 19746, '<td valign="top">You should put this into a tutorial called, "perspective" ;) <br/> <br/>Great use of super wide angle to accentuate the size of the digger thingy, the sky is dramatic and provides a good backdrop.  Bummer about the ISO but it came out fine after the noise editing software :)  I messed up a few good shots that way hehe.<br/> <br/>Kudos on your top 5, man :)</td>', 'You should put this into a tutorial called, "perspective" ;)  Great use of super wide angle to accentuate the size of the digger thingy, the sky is dramatic and provides a good backdrop.  Bummer about the ISO but it came out fine after the noise editing software :)  I messed up a few good shots that way hehe. Kudos on your top 5, man :)', '2005-06-15 06:12:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(1456946, 186876, 19746, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on your first blue!  It''s wonderful when an idea comes off :)  Very well done indeed<br/> <br/>Alex</td>', 'Congratulations on your first blue!  It''s wonderful when an idea comes off :)  Very well done indeed Alex', '2005-06-15 06:13:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(1456947, 186128, 34247, '<td valign="top">I have a kitten named Yoda...<br/> <br/>Feels too busy, and flat. My eyes are searching for a subject in the image. The crane is right there, but there''s too much competition. The yellow light box that obscures a part of the crane, the light fixtures on the right side, etc. The striped, sloped tent makes a nice counter point to the angling of the crane, but the stripes don''t quite work. I''d reckon crop in closer to the crane itself, highlight it as a singular object. I actually think there''s something interesting that could be done with the triangular black overhanging shape, as well.</td>', 'I have a kitten named Yoda... Feels too busy, and flat. My eyes are searching for a subject in the image. The crane is right there, but there''s too much competition. The yellow light box that obscures a part of the crane, the light fixtures on the right side, etc. The striped, sloped tent makes a nice counter point to the angling of the crane, but the stripes don''t quite work. I''d reckon crop in closer to the crane itself, highlight it as a singular object. I actually think there''s something interesting that could be done with the triangular black overhanging shape, as well.', '2005-06-15 06:14:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(1456956, 186605, 30018, '<td valign="top">Wow, you got robbed on this one dude.  I''m learning that in order to do well at dpchallenge, it seems you have to have a dramatic sky in the background.  That is such a shame.  This was an outstanding shot, and should have finished much higher.  Too many dramatic sky shots where the main subject is so much less interesting then this shot.  Get em next time...!</td>', 'Wow, you got robbed on this one dude.  I''m learning that in order to do well at dpchallenge, it seems you have to have a dramatic sky in the background.  That is such a shame.  This was an outstanding shot, and should have finished much higher.  Too many dramatic sky shots where the main subject is so much less interesting then this shot.  Get em next time...!', '2005-06-15 06:21:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(1456959, 186128, 35044, '<td valign="top">The image is interesting, but IMO falls a little betwen stools.  I like the repetition of angles in the roof and the crane, but to effectively featured that repetition as a central element, I would have included nothing but the roof and crane in the shot: the rest of the foreground clutters that part of the image. This may have been impractical (you would have had to have used a different shooting angle - I think probably by getting higher and closer to the roof line.  To create a more general image (not focussing solely on the repeated angles), the foreground needs to be better exposed and add interest to the shot.  This might easiest be done using the curves tool in PS (enabling you to lighten the dark areas without over exposing the bright areas).  <br/> <br/>The LHS of the image appears to add little to the photo and the crane is quite central (not always a good thing) - I would have played around with the composition a bit by cropping the photo in various ways to see if I could have improved it.  <br/> <br/>Overall, the idea is good, but the technical side (underexposing the foreground) and composition (not focussing hard on the interesting element (the angles), and/or leaving too much in the cluttered foreground) move this into the middle to low middle scores for me.<br/> <br/>Hope this helps explain one viewpoint!  Good luck in the future.</td>', 'The image is interesting, but IMO falls a little betwen stools.  I like the repetition of angles in the roof and the crane, but to effectively featured that repetition as a central element, I would have included nothing but the roof and crane in the shot: the rest of the foreground clutters that part of the image. This may have been impractical (you would have had to have used a different shooting angle - I think probably by getting higher and closer to the roof line.  To create a more general image (not focussing solely on the repeated angles), the foreground needs to be better exposed and add interest to the shot.  This might easiest be done using the curves tool in PS (enabling you to lighten the dark areas without over exposing the bright areas).   The LHS of the image appears to add little to the photo and the crane is quite central (not always a good thing) - I would have played around with the composition a bit by cropping the photo in various ways to see if I could have improved it.   Overall, the idea is good, but the technical side (underexposing the foreground) and composition (not focussing hard on the interesting element (the angles), and/or leaving too much in the cluttered foreground) move this into the middle to low middle scores for me. Hope this helps explain one viewpoint!  Good luck in the future.', '2005-06-15 06:27:25.000000', NULL, 0),
